#subtitle: International relations and dealing with Versailles.

= Foreign Policy

What should our foreign policy priority be?

@fp_menu

- @improve_west
- @improve_mexico
- @improve_soviet_1
- @improve_soviet_2
- @vatican_1
- @vatican_2
- @tanger_policy
- @root: Do not enact any policies for now.
- @cancel_advisor_action

@improve_west
title: Strengthen ties with France, Great Britain and the League of Nations.
choose-if: peseta_status = "orthodox"
unavailable-subtitle: It'll be difficult to approach France and Great Britain after abandoning the Gold Block Alignment.
on-arrival: west_relation += 2; economic_growth += 0.2; prr_relation += 3; dlr_relation += 3;

We reaffirm our commitment to the League of Nations and align our foreign policy with Western European democracies. Our diplomats advocate for disarmament and multilateral treaties.

France and Britain welcome our democratic stability, opening avenues for trade and commercial loans. Our bourgeois coalition partners approve of this orthodox international stance.

@improve_mexico
title: Improve our relations with President Cárdenas.
on-arrival: mexico_relation += 2; agricultural_exports += 1;

Mexico stands as our most enthusiastic ally in the Americas. President Lázaro Cárdenas' government shares our social-reformist vision and offers unconditional diplomatic backing in international forums.

@improve_soviet_1
title: Normalizes relations with Moscow.
subtitle: Could influence local communist dynamics...
max-visits: 1

Unlike most Western powers, the Republic has not yet fully normalized relations with the Soviet Union. Moscow is eager to open embassies and expand trade in the Mediterranean.

However, establishing ties with Stalin's government will alarm our conservative coalition partners and the military establishment.

- @soviet_trade_yes: Normalize relations and sign commercial agreements.
- @soviet_trade_pce: Normalize relations, using Moscow's influence to tame the PCE.
- @fp_menu: Do not normalize relations with the USSR at this time.

@soviet_trade_yes
on-arrival: soviet_relation += 2; economic_growth += 0.2; ejercito_loyalty -= 0.1; caballeristas_dissent -= 3; caballeristas_strenght += 5; coup_progress += 1; prr_relation -= 5; dlr_relation -= 5; other_right_republicans -= 5; foreign_goal_completed += 1; coalition_dissent += 1 if in_republican_socialist_conjunction

We exchange ambassadors with Moscow and sign trade agreements. The socialist left celebrates this step towards international working-class solidarity but Republican centrists and conservative officers view the Soviet presence with intense suspicion.

@soviet_trade_pce
on-arrival: soviet_relation += 2; pce_relation += 8*(1-dissent); ejercito_loyalty -= 0.1; caballeristas_dissent -= 3; caballeristas_strenght += 5; coup_progress += 1; prr_relation -= 5; dlr_relation -= 5; other_right_republicans -= 5; foreign_goal_completed += 1; coalition_dissent += 1 if in_republican_socialist_conjunction

In private diplomatic talks, we urge Moscow to instruct the PCE (Communist Party of Spain) to cease disruptive strikes and support the Republic's parliamentary framework. Following Comintern directives, the PCE tempers its attacks against the PSOE government, choosing instead to cooperate on broader anti-fascist fronts.

@improve_soviet_2
title: Normalizes relations with Moscow.
subtitle: Could influence local communist dynamics...
view-if: soviet_relation >= 2
on-arrival: soviet_relation += 1; pce_relation += 3*(1-dissent); caballeristas_dissent -= 3; caballeristas_strenght += 5

We've improved our relations with the Soviet Union.

@vatican_1
title: Open negotiations for a 'Modus Vivendi' with the Vatican.
subtitle: This will likely incur the wrath of our left republican allies.
view-if: modus_vivendi != 1
on-arrival: modus_vivendi = 1; polarization -= 10; coup_progress -= 1; catholics_psoe += 8; prr_relation += 5; dlr_relation += 5; other_right_republicans += 5; ar_relation -10; prss_relation -10; pce_relation -20; other_left_republicans_relation -10; coalition_dissent += 1; pce_coalition_dissent += 1; caballeristas_dissent += 10; besteiristas_dissent += 10; prietistas_dissent += 5;

We initiate discreet diplomatic channels with the Papal Nuncio. We offer guarantees regarding Church property rights in exchange for the Holy See recognizing the legal authority of the Republic.

While Catholics and conservatives welcome the gesture, left republicans like Manuel Azaña and secular socialist factions express immediate concern over compromising on constitutional principles.

@vatican_2
title: Sign a formal Concordat with the Holy See.
subtitle: We will face a vote of no confidence if we sign the Concordat.
choose-if: budget >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: We need at least 1 budget.
on-arrival: concordat = 1; budget -= 1; catholics_psoe += 10; polarization -= 15; coup_progress -= 2; prr_relation += 5; dlr_relation += 10; ar_relation -25; prss_relation -25; pce_relation -30; other_left_republicans_relation -15; other_right_republicans += 10; caballeristas_dissent += 10; besteiristas_dissent += 10; prietistas_dissent += 5; pro_republic += 20;
go-to: vote_of_no_confidence.vonc_menu
max-visits: 1

The Church secures guarantees for religious education and state stipends for clergy, while formally instructing Spanish bishops to respect the Republican constitution.

This agreement drastically undercuts the [+ ap_name +]'s crusade against the Republic and pacifies conservative circles. However, it triggers a political earthquake on the left. Azaña and the PRRS have called a Vote of No Confidence against this government.

@tanger_policy
title: Assert Spanish influence in the Tangier International Zone.
subtitle: Tangier is a hub for international finance, espionage, and arms smuggling.
max-visits: 1

As a co-protector of the Tangier International Zone alongside France and Britain, our Ministry of State can alter our posture in the city. We don't have a lot of influence here, so we'll be able to do just one policy.

- @tanger_security: Enforce strict anti-smuggling patrols to prevent arms trade.
- @tanger_finance: Turn Tangier into an open trade hub to generate state revenue.
- @fp_menu: Maintain the current status quo in Tangier.

@tanger_security
on-arrival: coup_progress -= 1 if guardia_civil_loyalty >= 0.65; west_relation -= 1; military_loyalty -= 0.1

We deploy additional Civil Guard and diplomatic inspectors to police the international zone. [? if guardia_civil_loyalty >= 0.65 : We dismantle secret financial accounts and intercept illegal arms shipments bound for conspiratorial military officers in Morocco. ?] [? if guardia_civil_loyalty < 0.65 : The smuggling hasn't been stopped, the Guardia Civil keeps looking to the other side ?] 

However, France and Britain complain about our heavy-handed unilateral actions in the neutral city. The army is also upset about this new measure.


@tanger_finance
on-arrival: budget += 1; economic_growth += 0.2; coup_progress += 1; ejercito_militancy += 0.5

We capitalize on Tangier's international status by lowering tariffs and easing banking regulations. Capital flows into Spanish-held banks in North Africa, providing much-needed revenue for the Treasury (+1 Budget).

However, relaxed oversight allows foreign agents and right-wing conspirators to operate in the city with impunity.
